    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>A lightweight dropdown on the WordPress dashboard that lets you switch between 1, 2, 3, or 4 column widget layouts instantly.</p>\n<h3>Usage</h3>\n<p>Simply select how many columns you want for your dashboard layout.</p>\n<h3>Support</h3>\n<p>If you have questions or issues, please reach out through our support channel at <a href=\"https://natechisley.com\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">NateChisley.com</a>. We’re happy to assist!</p>\n<h3>Contributing</h3>\n<p>We welcome contributions! Please follow our guidelines for contributing at <a href=\"https://natechisley.com\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">NateChisley.com</a>.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Log in to your WordPress site as an administrator.</li>\n<li>Go to the &#8220;Plugins&#8221; section in the WordPress dashboard.</li>\n<li>Click &#8220;Add New&#8221; and then click the &#8220;Upload Plugin&#8221; button.</li>\n<li>Choose the <code>admin-shift.zip</code> file from your computer and click &#8220;Install Now.&#8221;</li>\n<li>After installation is complete, click the &#8220;Activate Plugin&#8221; button.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Switch between 1, 2, 3, or 4 column widget layout in your admin dashboard instantly.",
